-- title:
--   Kernel of the cotangent transition map and p^v-torsion
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, let $p,h$ be natural numbers, and let $G$ be a $p$-divisible group of height $h$ over $R$ in the sense of the project's structure [`PDivisibleGroup`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L199): a family of commutative rings $G.\mathrm{level}\,v$ ($v\in\mathbb N$), each a cocommutative Hopf algebra over $R$ that is finite and free as an $R$-module, together with surjective $R$-coalgebra/algebra maps $G.\mathrm{transition}\,v\colon G.\mathrm{level}(v+1)\to G.\mathrm{level}\,v$, such that $\operatorname{rank}_R G.\mathrm{level}\,v=p^{vh}$ and the kernel of $G.\mathrm{transition}\,v$ is the ideal $\mathrm{torsionIdeal}$ of level $p^v$, i.e. the image of the augmentation ideal of $G.\mathrm{level}(v+1)$ under the algebra map induced by multiplication by $p^v$. For each $v$ write $I_v\subseteq G.\mathrm{level}\,v$ for the augmentation ideal, the kernel of the counit, and $G.\mathrm{Cotangent}\,v=I_v/I_v^2$ for its cotangent module; $G.\mathrm{cotangentMap}\,v$ is the $R$-linear map $I_{v+1}/I_{v+1}^2\to I_v/I_v^2$ induced by $G.\mathrm{transition}\,v$. The theorem asserts, for every $v\in\mathbb N$, the conjunction of two statements: the kernel of $G.\mathrm{cotangentMap}\,v$ equals the submodule $(p^v)\cdot(I_{v+1}/I_{v+1}^2)$ obtained by acting with the ideal of $R$ generated by $(p:R)^v$ on the whole cotangent module, and the corresponding action of that ideal on all of $I_v/I_v^2$ is zero.
--
--   This is the standard description of the cotangent spaces along the tower of a $p$-divisible group: $\omega_{G_v}$ is killed by $p^v$ and $\omega_{G_{v+1}}/p^v\omega_{G_{v+1}}\cong\omega_{G_v}$, valid over an arbitrary base ring with no hypothesis on $p$. It underlies the existence of a dimension for $G$, the computation of the rank of $G.\mathrm{level}\,v$ modulo $p^v$ in terms of the rank of $\omega_{G_1}$, and the freeness of the cotangent modules over Artinian base rings.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PDivisibleGroup_ker_cotangentMap_eq_smul_top_and_smul_top_eq_bot.lean

